+# SQLite schema v1
+
+`case_database.py` owns the schema and migration marker. The database is a rebuildable local index; `article.xml` and `meta.json` remain the source artifacts.
+
+| Table | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `schema_migrations` | Applied schema versions |
+| `articles` | Stable article identity, metadata, source hash, article-status provenance |
+| `sections` | Ordered, nested JATS section text and hashes |
+| `evidence_spans` | Exact section-local quote offsets bound to the source XML hash |
+| `concepts` | Optional original/normalized terminology mappings; not auto-populated yet |
+| `clinical_events` | Structured case events; schema is present, extraction is not yet shipped |
+| `assets` | Figure/table caption and reference inventory, with fail-closed reuse state |
+| `cards` | Generated card content and evidence references |
+| `card_claims` | Source-backed claim records created from imported evidence spans |
+| `review_decisions` | Append-only local decisions bound to card and evidence/source hashes |
+| `identity_conflicts` | Duplicate/conflicting PMID/DOI observations; records are not silently merged |
+| `guideline_sources`, `guideline_claims` | Separate future guideline layer, distinct from case-reported management |
+| `article_fts` | FTS5 index over title, abstract, and section text |
+
+`PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON` is enabled for every connection. `case_database.py check` runs SQLite integrity and foreign-key checks. The append-only triggers prevent ordinary SQL updates/deletes of review history but are not a security boundary against a database owner replacing or rebuilding the file.
